	Here's another vote for the old mac interface.  Right now I play
it over a vt100/9600 bps modem from my rs6k at work so I don't have to
deal with the mac interface.  Rather than just general griping, my
biggest problem is that the game slows me down.  My eyes have to keep
popping all over the place to keep track of everything.  

1) The normal messages "you hear the chime of a cash register", etc.
   appear in a separate window.  The critical viewing area of the
   game is the display, the stats below the display, and the messages at 
   the top.  These should be as close together as possible so my eyes 
   don't have to keep jumping back and forth between the display and the
   message window at the top of the screen.  When I'm in a battle, I
   don't want to have to keep scanning from the dungeon to a separate
   window to keep track of what's going on.  No matter how close I move
   the windows, it still further than the old interface.

2) The extra windows:  When I walk onto a spot with one item, I get a
   message in the normal message window saying what I see.  When there
   are multiple items, a little window pops up.  I like having that
   stuff in the main window, or at least in the same message window.
   Little windows popping up all over the place is really distracting.

3) Window placement: This may just be the fault of the unofficial
   compile, but the inventory window comes up with half the items off
   the bottom of the screen!  And there is an 'info' window when I start
   up that hangs way off the right side of the screen with just the edge
   showing on my display.  I have a IIci with the apple 13" color
   display.

4) The default font is hard to read, but not too horrible.  The large
   font would be fine if we could bring the status and the messages back
   into the main window, but with them in separate windows, my 13"
   screen is tight with the large font.  


	From what I've seen of the game so far it looks like this could
be a really great game, but I've been unable to play for more than half
an hour at a time without getting fed up with the interface.  And I've
played the last version for hours on end without any complaints. 

	On the positive side: I really like the walls and doors and
stuff in the new version.  

	Please, give us a compile option or a runtime option to use ONE
window!  Keep all the same mac graphics for the Dungeon display, but
give us the normal status bar and message display.  The old interface
wasn't broken, so don't fix it, or at least allow us the option of the
old interface.

	Thanks to the dev team for all the work that went into Nethack
3.1 and into the Mac interface.  Please take my comments as constructive
criticism on the interface, not as a slam on your effort in general.

